# Why this file exists BEFORE the first derivation does.
#
# This directory holds the per-release transient allow-lists that
# `../scripts/derive-transients.mjs derive` writes. It sits beside capture
# output, and an operator will be writing to it mid-session with a shell full
# of image paths, so it refuses every image byte form outright.
#
# The timing is the point (threat T-33-06). A directory that starts refusing
# images AFTER the first capture lands has already had one commit's worth of
# opportunity to leak one. So this file is committed before any derivation
# exists rather than added the first time somebody notices a stray image.
#
# The derived allow-lists themselves are deliberately NOT ignored: they are
# the committed artifacts this directory is for. Do not add a pattern here
# that would refuse them.

# Flat RAM captures and program images.
*.bin
*.prg
*.p00
*.raw

# Disk and tape images.
*.d64
*.d71
*.d81
*.g64
*.tap
*.t64

# Cartridge images and emulator snapshots.
*.crt
*.vsf

# Archives, which is how an image arrives when it does not arrive as itself.
*.zip
*.gz
*.7z
